The primary objective of this branch was to shift away from the **Table-Per-Hierarchy (TPH)** approach, where an abstract model served as the parent to three distinct classes: Part, Oil, and Gear. However, this approach posed challenges when attempting to directly access the Product table from the dbContext, given its abstract nature. As a result, a _major overhaul_ of the application's infrastructure was necessary. Beside modifying, deleting and adding new Data models, this included restructuring various components such as updating data seed classes, services, and MVC elements overall to align with the revised model. These adjustments were crucial to ensure smoother navigation and operation within the application. 

**Changes were applied to both the Core, Infrastructure and Web layer of the application, following the database overhaul:**
- IProductService interface no longer has a generic constraint;
- Services number was reduced from 3 (Part-, Oil-, GearService) to 1 (ProductService);
- Interface and Service's methods were modified, following the recent database updates.
- Enums number was reduced from 3 (Part-, Oil-, GearType) to 1 (ProductCategory);
- Infrastructure models were modified and each of them sorted in folders;
- Seeder classes were updated accordingly;
- Deleted old migrations and snapshot.

Hey, I didn't find how to get token scopes in editor. So there is an idea (;

During text decorating with `TextTransformation`, we already have token information here. So, we only need to include details to element `TextRunProperties` which we can read later whenever we need.

I didn't add any special method to read scopes, I use existing element properties:
```c#
private void Caret_PositionChanged(object sender, EventArgs e)
{
    var scopes = _textMateInstallation.EditorModel.GetTokenScopes(
        _textEditor.TextArea.Caret.Line - 1,
        _textEditor.TextArea.Caret.Column - 1);

    _statusTextBlock.Text = string.Format("Line {0} Column {1}. Scopes: {2}",
        _textEditor.TextArea.Caret.Line,
        _textEditor.TextArea.Caret.Column,
        scopes.Count > 0 ? string.Join(", ", scopes) : "None");
}
```

